@prefix dpv:  <https://w3id.org/dpv#> .
@prefix beam: <http://w3id.org/beam/core#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix dct:  <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix vann: <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/> .

<http://w3id.org/airiskkg/alignments/dpv>
    a owl:Ontology ;
    dct:title "DPV to BEAM Entity Alignment"@en ;
    dct:description """
    Alignment anchoring beam:Agent to DPV's entity vocabulary via
    rdfs:subClassOf. Scope is deliberately narrow (agreed 2026-07-15):
    DPV reuse in this project covers (a) data categories, handled entirely
    in the facet layer (ontology/facets/, hasPersonalDataCategory /
    hasIdentifiabilityLevel / data_facets closeMatches - see
    CHANGELOG_data_model.md), and (b) entities such as human and agent
    actors, handled here. DPV is NOT aligned to BEAM's Data/Model/Process/
    System classes - Tool4Boxology (ontology/alignments/
    tool4boxology_alignment.ttl) is the adapter for BEAM's general
    structural classes; it is a closer fit (same architecture-diagram
    domain) and is not duplicated here.

    Purely additive and machine-checkable interoperability (FAIR): this
    axiom is not consumed by motif SPARQL queries (no OWL reasoning runs
    during motif matching), so it cannot change any existing finding.
    """@en ;
    dct:source <https://w3id.org/dpv> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://w3c-cg.github.io/dpv/2.3/dpv/> ;
    vann:preferredNamespacePrefix "dpv" ;
    owl:imports <http://w3id.org/beam/core#> .

# --- Class alignment (verified against DPV v2.3, 2026-07-15) ---------------

beam:Agent rdfs:subClassOf dpv:Entity ;
    rdfs:comment "BEAM Agent aligned to DPV's Entity class ('a human or non-human thing that constitutes as an entity') - the correct breadth, since beam:Agent instances represent human actors (e.g. a human reviewer) as well as AI/software agents. Deliberately NOT aligned to the narrower dpv:Agent ('acting on behalf of another Entity, authorised to do so' - a delegated-authority relation, not what beam:Agent means) or to the AI extension's ai:AIAgent (would wrongly imply every beam:Agent, including human actors, is an AI agent)."@en .

# --- Checked, not aligned ----------------------------------------------------
#
# If BEAM ever splits beam:Agent into human vs. AI/software subtypes, the
# natural DPV anchors are already verified: dpv:NaturalPerson ("a human")
# for a human-actor subtype, and the DPV AI extension's ai:AIAgent ("a
# software agent that utilises AI technologies") for an AI-actor subtype.
# Not added now because no such BEAM subtypes exist yet (Rule R5: no
# speculative structure).
